      "message": "If we want to submit this, this must be split up in smaller CLs. In the current state, it\u0027s almost impossible to review (Python is not particularly readable and code moves combined with other changes make the diff very hard to follow). go/small-cls has great guidance on how to scope CLs if you haven\u0027t seen this yet.\n\nIn general, when moving larger amounts of code, it\u0027s good practice to put the move in one CL (even if it doesn\u0027t compile / work) and fixes in a follow up. This creates a much cleaner diff (and git history).\nAdditionally, putting those CLs in the same topic ensures that they are always submitted (and -- though not applicable here -- rolled back) together.",
